00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.590 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  hi i'm paul from krapow london today  we'll be making the quintessential thai  street food moopi mooping is grilled  pork we do a slightly different variant  we get chunks of the meat and then slow  cook it in a pan waiting for those  juices to be released and caramelised  down at the end creates a lovely little  glaze on the outside of the cuts so  within my background i've got no  classical training as a chef it's very  much a case of passed on from my family  spending time with both my grandmothers  both of them were crazy in the kitchen  that sunday roast dinner is where kind  of my family would all come together and  get probably their vegetable fix for the  weekend that was a requirement because  during the week we'd be kind of asian  food mad my dad had his way he would  genuinely have curry breakfast lunch and  dinner there's always been a passion for  asian cooking we use pork collar in our  variation of anything in thailand you  would generally get very thin little  slivers that would just get sort of  shown the coals just cook them through  and thus keep it tender we actually  started with getting collar steaks  slicing them up individually skewering  them all and then cooking them like that  but we found that a cooking time was  taking forever in the pan it was taking  so much longer on the skewers and having  to delicately turn each skewer all the  time so we switched it around to just  doing the chunks just keep them moving  around in the pan i think the benefit of  cooking in the pan plays more to the  western taste in western culture  everybody wants a good chunk of meat  which they can chew on they can get  their teeth stuck into cooking this at  home the demand primarily comes from the  guys down at the rugby club there are a  number of people there that have gained  an addiction to this somewhat akin to  crack so yeah we have to every now and  again cook up big batches and take that  up to the rugby club for a bit of a post  match  [Music]  that's moving  [Music]  you

